course: dictionary
lesson: 11203
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words can mean more than one thing, and the sentence tells you which meaning is right. «The wobbly table rocked when I put my cup on it.» A table that rocks is not firm, so wobbly means moving from side to side.
explain: The same word can describe a feeling or a voice. «Her legs felt wobbly after the fall» means her legs were shaky. «Her voice was wobbly as she said goodbye» means her voice shook because she was upset or nervous.
explain: Look at the words around the word before you decide. A «wobbly line» is not straight, but «throw a wobbly» is a special phrase meaning to get very angry or upset. When you are not sure, swap in your meaning and check that the sentence still makes sense.
fact: Wobbly is an adjective, and its comparison forms are wobblier and wobbliest.
fact: «Wobbly» means moving or shaking from side to side because it is not firm or steady.
fact: «Wobbly» can also mean shaky because you are tired, ill, scared or upset, as in «wobbly legs».
fact: A wobbly line is one that is not straight or neat.
fact: «Throw a wobbly» is informal, used in the UK, Australia and New Zealand, and means suddenly getting very angry or upset.
exercise: «My baby tooth is wobbly, so I wiggle it with my tongue.» What does wobbly mean here? | Long and thin | *Loose and moving from side to side | Very hungry | Bright and glowing
exercise: «Think of learning kick-ups: 3 on the first day, wobbly and wild.» What does wobbly suggest about the first day? | Wet and grey | *Shaky and unsteady | Calm and perfectly steady | Very loud and noisy
exercise: Jayden says his sister threw a wobbly when her toy broke. What does «threw a wobbly» mean? | Fell fast asleep | *Suddenly got very angry or upset | Did a dance on the stage | Dropped something heavy on the floor
test: «The wobbly chair made Sam nervous, so he sat on the floor.» What does wobbly mean here? | *Not firm, moving from side to side | Bright and shiny | Warm and soft | Very heavy and solid
test: «Her voice was wobbly as she said goodbye.» What does wobbly suggest about her voice? | *Shaky, because she was upset or nervous | Full and deep | Clear and loud | Slow and bored
exam: «A wobbly line is one that is...» | Thick and dark | Shiny and smooth | Straight | *Not straight or neat
